---
// The single idea to keep, if you keep one: the sound OF something, not FOR it.
// Full-bleed night block with a two-card contrast and a closing pull. The
// background image is a prop (defaults to svhgpt-04). Shared by everyone; the
// mode tag just reframes who it's addressed to.
interface Props {
  bgImg?: string;
}
const { bgImg = '/media/library/svhgpt-04-sound-of-not-for.webp' } = Astro.props;
---

<section class="wn-core">
  <div class="wn-core-bg" data-parallax data-parallax-speed="0.2" aria-hidden="true">
    <img src={bgImg} alt="" />
  </div>
  <div class="wn-core-inner">
    <div class="wn-mode-tag wn-reveal">
      What makes it different
      <span class="wn-mode-chip" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    </div>
    <h2 class="wn-core-head wn-reveal">
      The sound <em>of</em> something —<br />alongside the sound <em>for</em> it.
    </h2>
    <p class="wn-core-lead wn-reveal">
      Both are real, and both can be beautiful. They simply move in opposite
      directions — one comes <em>toward</em> you, the other comes <em>from</em> you.
    </p>

    <div class="wn-core-pair">
      <div class="wn-core-card wn-reveal">
        <div class="wn-core-kicker">Sound healing — sound for you</div>
        <h4>Beautiful sound, received</h4>
        <p>
          Singing bowls, tuning forks, a voice singing over you. You rest and let
          it wash through you — and it can be deeply soothing, restorative and
          real. A gift that comes <em>toward</em> you. Many people love it, and rightly so.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="wn-core-card wn-core-card--of wn-reveal" style="--wn-delay: 120ms">
        <div class="wn-core-kicker">Somatic Vocal Healing — sound of you</div>
        <h4>Your own state, given a voice</h4>
        <p>
          Here the sound comes <em>from</em> you. You make the sound <em>of</em> your
          tiredness, <em>of</em> the tightness in your chest, <em>of</em> the grief
          that's sat there a week. The healing is in the acknowledgment — in being
          present <em>with</em> what's there.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="wn-core-pull wn-reveal">
      Not better, not instead — a different doorway.
      <em>And when something is truly met, it stops needing to clamour.</em>
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
